findings.suggestedFix:
One server-side addition at registerNow's resync call site (Server/ws/hub.go:664-666) — do not put it inside sendVoicePeerKeys, since voice_join.go:531 shares that function and the joiner's own announce already comes from its client there:

    if voiceChID := c.getVoiceChID(); voiceChID != 0 {
        h.sendVoicePeerKeys(c, voiceChID)
        // Re-relay THIS client's own stored key back onto VoiceTopic so the
        // key holder's duplicate-announce branch re-wraps the CURRENT room
        // key for us — a rotation offer sent while this socket was down was
        // dropped and no replay tier can recover it.
        if key, sig := c.getE2EEPubKey(); key != "" {
            h.sendToVoiceChannelExcept(voiceChID, c.userID,
                buildVoiceE2EEAnnounce(c.userID, key, sig))
        }
    }

This needs no client change: handleAnnounceInner's dedup branch (livekitE2EE.ts:~812, "duplicate announce — will re-send offer if key holder") deliberately falls through to the wrap-and-offer branch on an identical key, so the holder re-offers the live room key. The announce is not blocked by _retiredPeerKeys (that set holds only keys a peer has been moved OFF of, never the live one) and re-runs verifyPeerAnnounce exactly as reannounceForReconnect's announce already does. Guard it on c.lastSeq > 0 if you want it strictly on the resume path.

